<% content_for :title, "#{@sheet.name} — Tinkerex" %>

<%# The grid library loads HERE ONLY, not in the global layout — it is a large bundle and no other
    page needs it. jsuites must precede jspreadsheet (see vendor/javascript/JSPREADSHEET-LICENSES.md).
    Classic script tags rather than importmap: these are UMD bundles that publish globals.

    "data-turbo-track": "reload" is NOT decoration copied from the layout — it is load-bearing, and
    its absence is a real bug that only shows up under Turbo Drive, not a hard page load. On a plain
    hard load, `yield :head` renders before `javascript_importmap_tags` and these classic tags block
    the parser, so they have always finished executing before Stimulus connects — that guarantee is
    what an earlier draft of this comment relied on. But every real path to this page (the sheets
    panel's `link_to`, and the create-sheet redirect) is a Turbo Drive VISIT, not a hard load: Turbo
    fetches the response and MERGES it into the live document rather than reparsing from scratch, and
    an untracked <script> merged into a live <head> loads asynchronously — Stimulus's
    MutationObserver routinely connects this page's controller (see sheet_controller.js) before that
    fetch finishes, so `window.jspreadsheet` isn't there yet. Reproduced live: a hard reload of a
    sheet page always found the library loaded; reaching the exact same page via the create-sheet
    redirect (a Turbo visit) hit "Grid failed to load" every time.

    `data-turbo-track="reload"` fixes the CAUSE, not the symptom: verified against the actual
    vendored bundle (turbo-rails' turbo.min.js) — Turbo hashes every `data-turbo-track="reload"`
    element into a `trackedElementSignature` per page and compares old vs. new before rendering
    (`trackedElementsAreIdentical`). The project page carries no such tags; this page does — so the
    signatures differ, `shouldRender` is false, and Turbo's `reload()` sets `window.location.href`
    itself: a REAL browser navigation, which re-parses from scratch and restores the hard-load
    guarantee instead of a soft merge. (This only protects entry/exit relative to a page that lacks
    these tags. Two sheet pages linked directly to each other would carry an IDENTICAL signature and
    would still race on a soft merge between them — moot today since nothing links sheet-to-sheet,
    but worth knowing before adding one.) %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <%= stylesheet_link_tag "jsuites", "jspreadsheet", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
  <%= javascript_include_tag "jsuites", "jspreadsheet", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
<% end %>

<nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Sheet path">
  <%= link_to "Projects", projects_path %>
  <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
  <%= link_to @sheet.project.name, project_path(@sheet.project) %>
  <span class="sep" aria-hidden="true">/</span>
  <span aria-current="page"><%= @sheet.name %></span>
</nav>

<%# The controller element wraps the HEAD AS WELL AS the grid: Stimulus resolves targets only
    within its own element's subtree, so a status span left up in the page head outside this div
    would never be found and the indicator would sit on "Saved" forever while saves failed. %>
<%# `cells`/`columns`, NOT the raw `data` attribute. Those readers exist precisely so a malformed or
    half-written blob renders an empty grid instead of something worse — and this page is the place
    they were written for. Passing raw `data` through meant a null entry in `columns` reached the
    Stimulus controller's `columns.map(c => c.title)` and threw, leaving a blank page with the status
    still reading "Saved". The controller permits `data: {}` wide open on purpose; the model is the
    guard, so the view has to actually ask it. %>
<div class="sheet-page"
     data-controller="sheet"
     data-sheet-url-value="<%= sheet_path(@sheet) %>"
     data-sheet-data-value="<%= { "columns" => @sheet.columns, "cells" => @sheet.cells }.to_json %>">

  <div class="page-head sheet-head">
    <div>
      <h1><%= @sheet.name %></h1>
      <span class="sheet-status muted" data-sheet-target="status">Saved</span>
    </div>
    <div class="head-actions">
      <%= form_with model: @sheet, scope: :sheet, url: sheet_path(@sheet), method: :patch,
                    class: "sheet-rename" do |f| %>
        <%= f.text_field :name, "aria-label": "Sheet name" %>
        <%= f.submit "Rename", class: "btn small" %>
      <% end %>
      <%= link_to "Export CSV", sheet_path(@sheet, format: :csv), class: "linkbtn" %>
      <%= button_to "Delete", sheet_path(@sheet), method: :delete, class: "linkbtn danger",
                    form: { data: { turbo_confirm: "Delete #{@sheet.name}?" } } %>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="sheet-grid" data-sheet-target="grid"></div>
</div>
